# Document reapplicable patches in docs/

Whenever you change files inside third-party / updatable plugins or themes (or any code that would be overwritten by an update), update the matching markdown under `docs/` in the same turn.

## Where to document

- Theme `dr-plus` patches → `docs/THEME-PATCHES-AFTER-UPDATE.md`
- Cross-cutting / multi-plugin reapply notes → `docs/MEDYAR-REAPPLY-PATCHES-AFTER-UPDATE.md`
- SMS / booking ownership notes → `docs/MEDYAR-SMS-BOOKING-AND-OWNERSHIP.md`
- New plugin or new concern → create `docs/<NAME>-PATCHES-AFTER-UPDATE.md` (or extend an existing file) and link it from the reapply index if one exists

## What each patch entry must include

1. Target path (plugin or theme + file)
2. Exact change (before/after snippet or clear surgical description)
3. Why it exists (so it can be re-judged after upstream updates)
4. How to re-apply after update (search markers / method names / hook names)

Do not rely on chat history alone. Prefer editing third-party code via child themes, mu-plugins, or custom plugins when possible; if a direct patch is unavoidable, it must be documented as above.
